WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768
-We're here with Jean Smart.
We're talking about "SNL."

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to ask --
they did a very funny

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.373
"Mare of Easttown" sketch
called "Murdur Durdur."

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you see it?

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Kate Winslet actually
sent it to me on my phone.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was hilarious!

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know how they put that
together so fast.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was brilliant.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.884 line:92%
-You have a wonderful show

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, it's very different
from "Hacks."

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:25.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it cool right now
to be working on two shows

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people are seeing
at the same time

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have such
different characters?

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, absolutely.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:32.966
It's fun, yeah, having the
both on at the same time.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:33.900 line:92%
And they're both so good.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm really proud
of both productions.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.806 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, you know, HBO.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love HBO.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.674 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They're very good to me.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] HBO has been
very good to you.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes.
-I mean, well, you've been
very good to HBO.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.415 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You elevate the work.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.582 line:92%
You elevate the work, Jean

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's it, that's it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.186 size:75% position:38%
-And Kate Winslet --
I can't say enough

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.120 line:92%
good things about Kate Winslet

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a doll.
She's just a doll.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing that is in common
in both shows is,

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've done some fantastic
iPad acting.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-Well, I'm just saying.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:09.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe you're playing
"Fruit Ninja"

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.137 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in "Mare of Easttown."

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.706 line:92%
You throw an iPad in "Hacks.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:17.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, was there
an iPad coach on set?

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.079 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.113 line:92%
No. There should have been

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
Should have been.
-Well, I figure
obviously self-coached,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.451 line:92%
because you don't need one

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, that was fun.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think this speaks to ho
seriously you take your acting

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.226 line:92%
But I heard that you actually --

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, this is
nothing funny about this.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.930 line:92%
You physically hurt yourself

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.032 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Was it on set of "Mare"?

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah, God.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apparently, I'll do anything
for a laugh.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a scene in the sho
where I'm sitting playing card

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
and drinking with the priest
as I do every week.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:54.781
And my phone rings, and I'
too lazy to get out of my chair.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I lean over
to the kitchen counter

00:01:55.882 --> 00:02:01.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get my phone, and I fal
on the floor, out of my chair.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.656 line:92%
They had a coach for that, too

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.624 line:92%
They had a stand-in to do that

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:09.529
I said, "I can fall out of m
own chair, thank you very much."

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.297 line:92%
So, there was another scen

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Kate and Guy
are going out on a date.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm playing her mother
so I'm craning my neck

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.672 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to spy on them.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:23.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm sitting on a railing
above the stairwell

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
that goes down
to the front door.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:30.416
And I thought it would be funn
if I pretended to almost fall.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.285 line:92%
It's just sort of Helen's thing.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the first five takes
went really well,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I leaned
just a little too far.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
The next take,
I went over the railing

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
and down the flight of stair
and broke my rib

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.698 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and got a concussion.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in the hospital
for five days.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Five days?
-Yeah.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.472 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And Kate was so sweet.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
She always called me "Mummy"
on the show,

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.608 line:92%
'cause I played her mother

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.076 size:75% position:38% line:92%
My back hurt so bad,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I hadn't just
cracked the rib.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.580 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It broke in half.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my back --
I thought I had broken my back

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was lying in a heap
at the bottom of the stairs,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.053 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and she was behind me

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of supporting my back
and she was saying...

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
[British accent]
"It's all right, Mummy.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're coming.
It's all right, Mummy."

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.261
[ Normal voice ] And I'm finally
in the ambulance,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the guy in the back
of the ambulance

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
is getting ready
to give me some morphine,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.267
and he says, "Boy, your daughter
was sure worried about you."

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.803 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I said, "My what?

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.372 size:88% position:44% line:92%
My daughter's not here."

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I went, "Oh, no.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.875 size:78% position:39% line:92%
No, she plays my d"--

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Didn't you
recognize her?"

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.312 line:92%
I said," That was Kate Winslet."

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.880 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he was like, "What?!

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.048 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I missed Kate Winslet?!"

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm going,
"Morphine, please!

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you can fan out late
after I get my drugs."

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He probably gave himself
morphine to get over

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
the pain of having missed
Kate Winslet.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.227 line:92%
So, they obviously must have

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
had to change the whole
shooting schedule

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
thanks to you
going down the stairs.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:55.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Unbelievably --
unbelievably -- they didn't,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I actually wrapped
on schedule.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because when I fell
down the stairs,

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was five minutes away
from going to the airport,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I had four days off
and I was gonna go home

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and see my family.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
But instead, I spent five days
in the hospital.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I had to quarantin
for three days,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.552 line:92%
which was most of that weekend

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:18.291
And I went back on schedul
on a lot of pills [Chuckles]

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:21.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
and finished my last
few days' work.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it would
have been great if
that was your last shot,

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and while you were just
lying in a heap,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
you heard,
"That's a wrap on Jean."

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:33.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I do recall yelling,
"I hope you got that on film!"

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.008 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, people have bee
saying recently,

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:42.081
this is the Jean Smart-aissance,
because we've seen you

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
in so many critically acclaime
shows recently.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.487
Do you feel like you're living
through the Jean Smart-aissance,

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.757 size:88% position:44%
or is this just business
as usual for an actor?

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, first of all,
I challenge you to spell that.

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:57.497 line:92%
But, no, I mean, I just --

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.499 size:78% position:39%
You know, I feel like
I hit the jackpot,

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't take it
for granted at all --

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially at this
late stage of the game.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:10.176
No, I've just been given so many
extraordinary opportunitie

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last few years
that it kind of led to this.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is just like
a dream job.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
If they had given me a paper
and pencil and said,

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Describe your next job
that you want --

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything you want,"
it would have been this job.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it's interesting,
'cause the clip we showed

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
of "Hacks," you obviously
are playing someone

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:29.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
who talks about how
it never gets easier.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's talking about
stand-up comedy,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.335
but have you found, as you
career has sort of expande

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you've done all these
different things --

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.772 line:92%
has it gotten easier for you

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.040 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, it has.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I don't think I'm
necessarily a better actor now

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.813 line:92%
than I was 20 or 30 years ago.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:49.182 line:92%
The thing about actors is --

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:55.455
and even that tiny percentag
of actors who work a lot -

00:05:55.455 --> 00:06:00.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
even most of them,
I would dare say,

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:04.430
rarely get the chance to sho
what they really are capable of.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.234
Most actors never, ever ge
the chance to show what they do.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, other people
like painters and singers

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.741 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and dancers and writers,

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
they can do it
any time they want.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.478 size:81% position:41%
Doesn't mean they'll
get paid, necessarily,

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:19.779 line:92%
but they can actually do it.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:24.083
But as an actor, you have to
sort of be given permissio

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to do your work.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, invited
to do your work.

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:31.758 size:78% position:39%
-Well, I want to give
my great gratitude

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:34.127 size:88% position:44%
to everyone who has been
sending you invitations

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:37.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
in recent years, because it ha
been so much fun to watch.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a pleasure
to see you, Jean.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for being here.
-Thank you.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.001 line:92%
You, too, Seth. Thank you.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Hacks" is streaming
on HBO Max.

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:46.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

